# Panel source patch — phase 1 / task 2 remediation (G-1..G-6)
# Applies at panel-src root:  patch -p1 < this.patch
# Base: git commit bd9c80b (medpad-full-1.9/inst-stage/panel-src)
#        WITH patches/panel-src-phase1-task1.patch already applied.
# After applying: npm install (or npm ci && npm i next@16.4.3 --save-exact)
#        then npx prisma generate && npm run build.
# Contents (cumulative — grows with each remediation commit):
#   G-1  customer authorization: app/customers list returns only ASSIGNED
#        customers; app PUT /api/app/customers/[id] and app check-in enforce
#        server-side assignment (403 otherwise).
#   G-2  app-token expiry + revocation: AppToken.expiresAt/revokedAt,
#        admin-configurable TTL (appTokenTtlHours, 0..8760, default 720h,
#        0 = never), admin settings API + revoke endpoint, src/lib/settings.ts,
#        src/instrumentation.ts runtime migration for existing databases.
#   G-5  admin logout requires a valid admin session; /api/logout scope
#        'current' and /api/logout-all scope 'all' as separate endpoints.
#   G-3  employee lifecycle: validated edit, deactivate/reactivate (token
#        revocation, history preserved), password reset (revokes tokens),
#        AuditLog model + /api/audit-log viewer + audit writes on
#        create/update/lifecycle/revoke/settings, full EmployeesTab UI.
#   G-4  audio authorization: own-record + assigned-customer only; orphaned
#        files employee-denied (404) with an admin-only review listing
#        (GET /api/admin/media-orphans); installer now preserves the RUNTIME
#        uploads dir (panel/.next/standalone/uploads) across updates.
#   (this file is regenerated per commit; see WORKLOG for per-commit state)
